  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to repatriated people from Dominican Republic in the border north-east of Haiti</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support 1200 rapatriated people by offering dignified assistance (food, transport, health kits, clothing and underwear and accommodation)&#xa0; and strengthening the SJM-Haiti reception centre during the period of implementation.
During the period April 1, 2025 - May 31, 2025, the project has provided support to 423 repatriated migrants in different way based on specific need identified:

147 people received assistance to cover transport costs form the border to where they are from in Haiti.
125 people received food assistance;
101 people received health kits.
42 people received clothing and underwear.

An extension is agreed to allow to complete 100% of project activities planned</narrative>
  </description>
